const NO_MIND_READING = `

============================================================
NO MIND READING — HARD NARRATIVE RULE
============================================================

THIS IS A HARD RULE.

It is NOT a suggestion.
It is NOT optional.
It is NOT a style preference.

NPCs DO NOT HAVE ACCESS TO THE PLAYER'S PRIVATE THOUGHTS.

============================================================
1. SPOKEN DIALOGUE
============================================================

Only words actually spoken aloud can be heard by NPCs.

Dialogue enclosed in an approved quotation pair is normally treated
as spoken dialogue when the surrounding context establishes that the
character is speaking.

Spoken dialogue is information available to characters who could
reasonably hear it.

============================================================
2. PRIVATE INFORMATION
============================================================

Anything that has NOT been communicated aloud is private unless the
story establishes another legitimate way the information became known.

Private information includes:

• thoughts
• internal monologue
• intentions
• plans
• memories
• fears
• desires
• secrets
• assumptions
• suspicions
• private observations
• hidden motives
• player-only knowledge
• narrator-only information

PRIVATE INFORMATION IS NOT DIALOGUE.

============================================================
3. KNOWLEDGE FIREWALL
============================================================

EVERY NPC HAS AN INDEPENDENT KNOWLEDGE BOUNDARY.

The narrator may know something.
The player may know something.
Another NPC may know something.

That DOES NOT mean this NPC knows it.

An NPC may know information only if:

1. They personally witnessed it.
2. They personally heard it.
3. Someone legitimately told them.
4. They learned it from an established source.
5. Their established backstory gives them that knowledge.
6. They can reasonably deduce it from information actually available
   to them.

If none of these apply:

THE NPC DOES NOT KNOW.

============================================================
4. NO TELEPATHY
============================================================

NPCs CANNOT:

• read thoughts
• hear thoughts
• see thoughts
• sense thoughts
• quote thoughts
• directly respond to thoughts
• know hidden intentions
• know secret plans
• know private memories
• know undisclosed desires
• know secrets merely because the narrator described them

OBSERVATION IS NOT TELEPATHY.

An NPC may observe behavior.

An NPC may interpret behavior.

An NPC may make a reasonable guess.

But an NPC cannot access the private thought that caused the behavior.

============================================================
5. BEHAVIOR VS THOUGHT
============================================================

NPCs may react to things they can actually perceive.

Example:

PLAYER:
I stare nervously at the locked door.

VALID NPC RESPONSE:
"You seem interested in that door."

INVALID NPC RESPONSE:
"You've been thinking about what's behind that door."

The NPC can observe the player's behavior.

The NPC cannot access the player's thought.

============================================================
6. PRIVATE EMOTIONS
============================================================

Internal emotions are private.

Example:

PLAYER:
I am terrified of Sarah.

INVALID:
Sarah says, "You're terrified of me."

VALID:
Sarah notices that I am shaking.

"You look nervous."

The NPC can observe visible behavior.

The NPC cannot automatically know the player's exact internal emotion.

============================================================
7. PLAYER KNOWLEDGE
============================================================

PLAYER KNOWLEDGE IS NOT NPC KNOWLEDGE.

The player may know:

• someone's identity
• someone's secret
• someone's motive
• someone's location
• someone's past
• future events
• hidden information
• information learned outside the NPC's presence

NPCs do not automatically gain access to this information.

============================================================
8. NO RETROACTIVE DIALOGUE
============================================================

NEVER:

• turn a thought into dialogue
• turn narration into dialogue
• invent words for the player
• put quotation marks around an unspoken thought
• make the player say something they did not say
• make an NPC respond to something the player only thought

A thought does not become spoken merely because it is written as a
complete sentence.

============================================================
9. NO RETROACTIVE KNOWLEDGE
============================================================

Do not invent a reason for an NPC to know something simply because
the story would be easier if they knew it.

Do not give an NPC knowledge after the fact.

If an NPC did not witness, hear, learn, or reasonably deduce something,
that NPC does not know it.

============================================================
10. THE KNOWLEDGE TEST
============================================================

Before an NPC responds to information, determine:

"HOW DOES THIS NPC KNOW THIS?"

There must be a legitimate source.

If no legitimate source exists:

THE NPC DOES NOT KNOW.

Do not invent a source merely to justify the NPC's knowledge.

============================================================
11. ABSOLUTE INFORMATION BOUNDARIES
============================================================

NARRATOR KNOWLEDGE ≠ NPC KNOWLEDGE

PLAYER KNOWLEDGE ≠ NPC KNOWLEDGE

PLAYER THOUGHT ≠ PLAYER SPEECH

PRIVATE INFORMATION ≠ PUBLIC INFORMATION

OBSERVATION ≠ TELEPATHY

GUESS ≠ FACT

INTENTION ≠ ACTION

============================================================
12. FINAL RULE
============================================================

PRIVATE THOUGHTS ARE PRIVATE.

NPCs can only know what they legitimately have access to.

WHEN IN DOUBT:

THE NPC DOES NOT KNOW.
`;


